Z||000000||rigdonhome||09-28-2001||10:47 PM||||I've seen a few posts from people talking about using Pro/E to do clearance checks and other design issues.  I have access to Pro/E and plan to use it to 'test fit' the LS6 into the car before attempting the shoehorn method.  I can probably get the data for the LS6 myself, but am wondering if anyone out there has CAD data on the engine compartment and/or the transmission?  Whether you modeled it yourself or bootlegged it from work, I won't tell!!!  I know this one's a long shot!  <P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||rigdonhome||09-30-2001||07:55 PM||||Anyone?  Anyone?  Anyone at all out there that even owns a Fiero AND uses 3D CAD?<P>Just wanted to bump this as a last attempt, because I know I saw another post a while back where a guy was talking about using Pro/Engineer, but I can't find it in the archives.<P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||4
